    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "**Spec point** — `spcpt_5ssGMTjjDQvqsgHC`",
    "reading_order" : 2,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "paragraph",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000003",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "Physical Properties & Intermolecular Forces",
    "reading_order" : 3,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "heading",
    "heading_level" : 2,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000004",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "Branching",
    "reading_order" : 4,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "heading",
    "heading_level" : 4,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000005",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "The larger the surface area of a molecule, the more contact it will have with adjacent molecules",
    "reading_order" : 5,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000006",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "The surface area of a molecule is **reduced by branching**",
    "reading_order" : 6,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000007",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "The greater its ability to induce a dipole in an adjacent molecule, the greater the** London (dispersion) forces** and the higher the melting and boiling points",
    "reading_order" : 7,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000008",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "This point can be illustrated by comparing different isomers containing the same number of electrons:",
    "reading_order" : 8,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000010",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "***Boiling points of molecules with the same numbers of electrons but different surface areas***",
    "reading_order" : 10,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "paragraph",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000011",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "Number of electrons",
    "reading_order" : 11,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "heading",
    "heading_level" : 4,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000012",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "The greater the number of electrons (or the greater the molecular mass) in a molecule, the greater the likelihood of a distortion and thus the greater the frequency and magnitude of the temporary dipoles",
    "reading_order" : 12,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000013",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "The dispersion forces between the molecules are stronger and the enthalpy of vaporisation, melting and boiling points are larger",
    "reading_order" : 13,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000014",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "The greater boiling points of the noble gases illustrate this factor:",
    "reading_order" : 14,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000016",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "***As the number of electrons increases more energy is needed to overcome the forces of attraction between the noble gases atoms***",
    "reading_order" : 16,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "paragraph",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000018",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "***Graph showing the increase in boiling point as the number of electrons increases***",
    "reading_order" : 18,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "paragraph",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000019",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "Alcohols",
    "reading_order" : 19,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "heading",
    "heading_level" : 4,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000020",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "Hydrogen bonding occurs between molecules where you have a hydrogen atom attached to one of the very electronegative elements - fluorine, **oxygen** or nitrogen",
    "reading_order" : 20,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000021",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "In an alcohol, there are **O-H bonds** present in the structure",
    "reading_order" : 21,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000022",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "Therefore hydrogen bonds set up between the slightly positive hydrogen atoms (δ+ H) and lone pairs on oxygens in other molecules",
    "reading_order" : 22,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000023",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "The hydrogen atoms are slightly positive because the bonding electrons are pulled away from them towards the very electronegative oxygen atoms",
    "reading_order" : 23,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000024",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "In **alkanes**, the only intermolecular forces are **temporary induced dipole-dipole forces**",
    "reading_order" : 24,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000025",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "Hydrogen bonds are much stronger than these and therefore it takes more energy to separate alcohol molecules than it does to separate alkane molecules",
    "reading_order" : 25,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000026",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "Therefore, the boiling point of alkanes is lower than the boiling point of the respective alcohols",
    "reading_order" : 26,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000027",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "For example, the boiling point of propane is -42 <sup>o</sup>C and the boiling point of propanol is 97 <sup>o</sup>C",
    "reading_order" : 27,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000028",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "Hydrogen Halides",
    "reading_order" : 28,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "heading",
    "heading_level" : 4,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000029",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "The boiling points of the hydrogen halides are as follows",
    "reading_order" : 29,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000031",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "The boiling points of the rest of the hydrogen halides **increase** as the molecules become larger",
    "reading_order" : 31,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000032",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "The extra electrons allow greater temporary dipoles and so increase the amount of London dispersion forces between the molecules",
    "reading_order" : 32,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000033",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "Hydrogen fluoride also has hydrogen bonding between the HF molecules",
    "reading_order" : 33,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000034",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "The bond is very polar so that the hydrogen has a significant amount of positive charge and the fluorine a significant amount of negative charge. In addition, the fluorine has small intense lone pairs",
    "reading_order" : 34,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000035",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "Hydrogen bonds can form between the hydrogen on one molecule and a lone pair on the fluorine in its neighbour",
    "reading_order" : 35,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  } ],
